      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town hall in Saint\u2011Gilles showcases impressive Gothic Revival architecture, a prominent landmark that reflects the municipality\u2019s historic character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/belgium/brussels-capital_saint-gilles",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Saint\u2011Gilles is one of the 19 municipalities of the Brussels\u2011Capital Region, legally bilingual but predominantly French\u2011speaking today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint-Gilles%2C_Belgium",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The street pattern of Saint\u2011Gilles was completely remodelled in the 1860s by architect and urbanist Victor Besme, shaping the area\u2019s modern layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint-Gilles%2C_Belgium",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The name Saint\u2011Gilles comes from its patron saint and main church, a tradition that dates back to the village\u2019s early history.",
